# Interest signup & Mailchimp

Read `docs/agent/MAILCHIMP-SIGNUP.md` before changing the signup form or subscribe API.

The July 2026 clinic is over. The form now captures an ongoing interest list
(tag `Interest List - 2026`), not registrations for a specific event.

## Data model (parent + child ages)

- **Parent record** at real email, `ROLE = Parent`, `CHLDAGES` = comma-separated ages
- **Child records** at `clinic-{hash}-{N}@brooklyngamebreakers.com`, `ROLE = Player`, individual `AGE`
- Keep the `clinic-` alias prefix — changing it duplicates rows for returning parents
- Do not put all children on aliases only — parent must keep real email for campaigns
- Do not use email subaddressing (`+bgaclinic2`) — Mailchimp rejects it

## Merge tags (max 10 chars)

Use `PEMAIL`, `PNAME`, `CHINDEX`, `CHCOUNT`, `CHLDAGES`, `SIGNUPID` — never `PARENT_EMAIL` or `PARENT_EMAI`.

New merge fields must be created by hand in the Mailchimp dashboard first. Tags
are created automatically by the API, so prefer a tag for new categorization.

## Segments

- Interest list: `Interest List - 2026` tag
- July clinic attendees: `Flag Football Clinic - July 2026` tag (historical, no longer applied)
- Age counts: `ROLE = Player` (child alias rows only)
- Campaigns: `ROLE = Parent` or exclude emails containing `clinic-`

## Local dev

`npm run dev` proxies `/api` to production — **form submissions write to the live
audience.** Use `MOCK_API=1 npm run dev` to serve `/api/subscribe` locally instead.
Restart the dev server after `vite.config.js` changes.
